  "program_1343": {
    "summary": "Ground floor of the consistorium in the merchant-house pattern (diele, dornse, cellar; dossier: 'first-quarter-14th-century cellar and diele-dornse expansion precede 1343').",
    "rooms": {
      "diele": "great hall entered from the market portal: public business, the Vogt's lower court (first instance under Lübeck law) with assessors, litigants and oath-helpers before the barrier, oaths on the lectern, petitioners waiting, the Kämmerer receiving fines at the counting table; cellar hatch to the store below",
      "dornse": "heated council chamber (hypocaust vents, attested type in Reval dornse): the sitting council with two burgomasters, the town seal and wax on the table, the scribe at the window desk, the town books in the cupboard, privileges and seal in the three-lock chest"
    },
